course: dictionary
lesson: 2290
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Cricket» can mean a bat-and-ball game, or a small jumping insect. The words around it give you the clues to choose the right meaning.
explain: «In cricket the bowler keeps the arm straight, and the umpire will not allow it.» Bowler, umpire and arm are all clues that cricket means the game. Ask yourself: does this make sense as a game?
explain: «At a night market in Thailand a child your age buys a paper cone of fried crickets.» You cannot fry a game, and people buy fried food. So here cricket must mean the insect. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Cricket is a bat-and-ball game played by two teams of eleven players.
fact: In cricket, a bowler bowls the ball to a batter, who tries to score runs.
fact: A cricket is a jumping insect, a bit like a grasshopper.
fact: A cricket makes its chirping sound by rubbing its wings together.
fact: Male crickets chirp faster when it is warmer.
exercise: «Let's play cricket after school.» What does cricket mean here? | A type of fish | A jumping insect that chirps in the grass | A small pet kept in a glass tank | *A bat-and-ball game played by two teams
exercise: «We heard a cricket chirping in the long grass at night.» What does cricket mean here? | A kind of bat used for hitting | A bat-and-ball game with eleven players | A wooden stump in the ground | *A jumping insect that chirps by rubbing its wings
exercise: In cricket, what does the bowler do? | Sings loudly to the crowd | Jumps and chirps in the grass | Keeps the score on a board | *Bowls the ball to a batter, who tries to score runs
test: «The batter hit the ball over the rope in the air for a big score.» In cricket, what is that hit worth? | Two | Four | *Six | One
test: «Crickets chirp faster when it is warm.» What does cricket mean here? | A bat-and-ball game on a large field | *A jumping insect like a grasshopper | A wicket and a set of stumps | An umpire in a white coat
exam: «The cricket jumped off the leaf and chirped all evening.» Which word is the best clue that cricket means an insect here? | Umpire | Eleven | *Chirped | Field
